  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A ball of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is dropped from the height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The height, at which the magnitude of velocity becomes equal to the magnitude of acceleration due to gravity, is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. [Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> ]",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/9e89e5d4-9b8b-4493-b1de-0986b827ac0a-image.png\" style=\"width: 130px; height: 116px;\" /></p><p>Consider downward direction to be positive.</p><p>Applying first equation of motion,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Distance covered in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>g</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>Hence, height of the point from the surface&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
